# Mode two, the ruling: Bot2 gives Llanowar Elves hexproof in response (Snakeskin Veil, which also adds a counter), so the
# creature you don't control is an illegal target as Archdruid's Charm resolves. The Elvish Mystic still gets its +1/+1 counter
# but no damage is dealt: the Elves (now 2/2) have none marked.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Elvish Mystic
Archdruid's Charm
Plains x3
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Snakeskin Veil
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Archdruid's Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Target(Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Snakeskin Veil.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Power = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Damage = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 2
Stack.Count = 0
